+Bounded architecture audit and selected contract:
+
+- Node awaits recovered rows through a one-row sink. During room reopen that
+  sink first buffers authenticated rows until snapshot/authority/projection
+  validation completes; the room then calls the required external
+  `onAcceptedVertex` once per staged row before publishing its in-memory
+  candidate. A later callback rejection cannot undo an earlier arbitrary
+  external effect. A later process has no durable application-delivery cursor
+  and reconstructs the retained rows again.
+- The live journal durably owns admission, not consumption by an arbitrary
+  application callback. The settlement plan owns replacement issuance, not
+  application effects. The room-head record owns authenticated epoch state,
+  not per-consumer delivery acknowledgement. Moving in-memory map/projection
+  updates, reordering callbacks, or storing a receipt immediately before or
+  after a callback cannot atomically couple unknown external state with that
+  receipt: before risks omission and after risks duplication.
+- The selected narrow contract therefore distinguishes authoritative state
+  from notification. Canonical application state is the deterministic
+  `projectAcceptedOperations`/`onProjection` result and admits every
+  authenticated vertex exactly once by digest. `onAcceptedVertex` is an
+  authenticated **replayable notification attempt**: it may be invoked again
+  after its own rejection, session failure, crash or cold reopen. A consumer
+  that persists side effects must idempotently key them on the authenticated
+  vertex digest already present in `AdmittedReceivedVertexView`; callback
+  order remains canonical within one attempt. Throw/rejection remains
+  fail-closed for that session, cleanup remains mandatory, and no public issue
+  or active owner is exposed before successful recovery. This clarification
+  does not authorize swallowing callback errors, losing a retained row,
+  duplicating canonical state, retrying an unclassified signed issue, or
+  treating a callback as an authority source.
+- Current production examples do not depend on external exactly-once callback
+  effects: v3-chat and grid use `onAcceptedVertex` as a no-op and derive live
+  state from `onProjection`; the room's migration-local collectors are
+  bounded reconstruction observers whose results are checked against
+  canonical projection/state. GREEN must source-audit every current consumer
+  and pin this inventory. Any consumer that proves an un-idempotent durable
+  side effect is a blocking contradiction and forces the transactional-port
+  reslice below.
+- Rejected alternatives: swallow callback failure (silent loss), mark a local
+  receipt before callback (at-most-once omission), mark it after callback
+  (the demonstrated duplicate window), or claim failure atomicity by moving
+  only room-local map writes (does not roll back external state). A true
+  exactly-once external-effect guarantee requires an application-owned atomic
+  batch/idempotency port whose effect and durable receipt commit on one storage
+  boundary, plus restart, corruption, prune and compatibility ownership. That
+  is a public API/schema design and is expressly not folded into f5b0u.
+
+Tests-only GREEN acceptance for the selected contract:
+
+1. Preserve the genuine two-row, second-callback failure and same-room cold
+   reopen. Replace neither its authority nor its durable data. Prove the first
+   session rejects and releases transport/owner custody, the second session
+   authenticates and opens, and callback attempts are explicitly observed as
+   replayable `d1,d1,d2` rather than mislabeled as an exactly-once external
+   effect.
+2. In the same test, keep hard exact-once assertions for canonical projected
+   operation IDs, application-state bytes, durable issuance rows and room
+   authority. A mutant that duplicates `d1` in canonical state must fail even
+   though repeated notification attempts are permitted.
+3. Add the exact public-contract comment beside
+   `CreateV3RoomSessionInput.onAcceptedVertex`, and a source/type assertion
+   pinning digest-keyed idempotency guidance and fail-closed rejection. Do not
+   change the callback's field shape, return type, runtime ordering, error
+   behavior or export surface.
+4. Audit all production consumers and pin that none treats the callback as a
+   durable exactly-once commit. Preserve v3-chat/grid behavior byte-for-byte
+   and retain the existing first-callback sink/commit failure controls.
+5. Run the focused successor-replay suite, source-governance suite, affected
+   room/Node builds and typechecks, exact-owner lint/format/diff/source-shape
+   checks, retained room/recovery/creator-successor/active-owner suites and a
+   clean-isolated checkout. Record commands, complete results, consumer
+   inventory, hashes and a self-excluding manifest.
+
+Because this deliberately corrects a public callback semantic overclaim next
+to authenticated recovery, one bounded Grok 4.6/high, Codex
+`gpt-5.6-sol` high and Fable xhigh plan review is mandatory before changing
+the RED expectation or public-contract comment. Invoke Fable only through the
+interactive `claude-phel` alias. Only P0/P1 blocks; every P2 receives an owner
